# GitHub Repo Creation Skill

Streamline new GitHub repo creation. Guides manual GitHub steps + automates local setup.

## Usage

```
/code-git-create-repo <project-name> [--public|--private] [--description "..."]
```

## Workflow

### Step 1: Create on GitHub (Manual)
1. Go to github.com/new
2. Enter repository name: `{project-name}`
3. Visibility: public/private (default: public)
4. Description: (optional)
5. Click "Create repository"
6. Copy URL: `https://github.com/[username]/[repo].git`

### Step 2: Local Setup (Automated)
```bash
# Script auto-generates these:
cd /path/to/project
git init
git config user.email "your-email@example.com"
git config user.name "Your Name"
echo "# {project-name}" > README.md
echo "node_modules/" >> .gitignore
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit: {project-name} setup"
```

### Step 3: Connect & Push (Automated)
```bash
git remote add origin https://github.com/[username]/[repo].git
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
```

## Options

### Public Repository
```
/code-git-create-repo my-project --public
```

### Private Repository
```
/code-git-create-repo my-project --private
```

### With Description
```
/code-git-create-repo my-project --description "My awesome project"
```

## What Happens

**Manual (User):**
- ✓ Create repo on GitHub
- ✓ Copy repo URL
- ✓ Share URL with skill

**Automated (Skill):**
- ✓ Initialize local git
- ✓ Create .gitignore
- ✓ Create README.md
- ✓ Make initial commit
- ✓ Add remote
- ✓ Push to GitHub

## Requirements

- Git installed locally
- GitHub account
- Shell access

## Example

```bash
/code-git-create-repo my-awesome-tool --public --description "Developer tool for CLI automation"

# Output:
# Step 1: Create on GitHub
#   Go to: https://github.com/new
#   Name: my-awesome-tool
#   Visibility: Public
#
# Step 2: Created repo? Paste URL below
#   > https://github.com/pauldx/my-awesome-tool.git
#
# Step 3: Initializing local repo...
#   ✓ Git initialized
#   ✓ .gitignore created
#   ✓ README.md created
#   ✓ Initial commit done
#   ✓ Remote added
#   ✓ Pushed to GitHub
#
# Done! Repo ready at: https://github.com/pauldx/my-awesome-tool
```

## Helper Script

See: `skills/code-git-create-repo/setup.sh`

## Limitations

- ⚠️ GitHub repo must be created manually (for security)
- Cannot auto-generate licenses (use GitHub UI)
- Cannot configure branch protection (manual)
- Cannot set up CI/CD (use GitHub Actions)

